      "value": "@{5de9405aea7cc52772fcc359|full_name}: to be fair, this was made very early in the closed alpha of udon. I don't think this is super necessary anymore, as most of the functions I would have used this for have been covered. I may be wrong though as there are always edge cases, especially on stuff like cameras which seem to be protected components even if they're added by the world. But that should be its own canny, rather than going through a roundabout method like UI buttons.",
      "viewerReactions": null
